  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Well, I mean, I am technically still a student, majoring in computer science.",
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.37,
      "duration": 4.37
    },
    {
      "text": "But here is the thing: I actually started out studying chemistry, and I switched majors later on, which kind of changed my whole university experience.",
      "start": 4.37,
      "end": 13.17,
      "duration": 8.8
    },
    {
      "text": "[slight pause] And you know, going through that taught me something important: you have to keep asking yourself what you really want.",
      "start": 13.17,
      "end": 20.04,
      "duration": 6.87
    },
    {
      "text": "Like, actually want, not just what sounds good on paper.",
      "start": 20.04,
      "end": 23.19,
      "duration": 3.15
    },
    {
      "text": "It was a bit scary at the time, honestly, because I had already spent over a year in chemistry.",
      "start": 23.19,
      "end": 28.49,
      "duration": 5.3
    },
    {
      "text": "But I just was not into it, so I made up my mind and switched to computer science.",
      "start": 28.49,
      "end": 33.0,
      "duration": 4.51
    },
    {
      "text": "And looking back now, it was probably one of the best decisions I made in college.",
      "start": 33.0,
      "end": 37.64,
      "duration": 4.64
    },
    {
      "text": "So yeah, that is where I am now, and I am pretty happy with how things turned out.",
      "start": 37.99,
      "end": 43.16,
      "duration": 5.17
    }
  ],
